Alkali metals have very low ionisation energy. So, it will be very easy to eject an electron. Electrons are ejected from the surface of the metal when a radiation of suitable frequency is used in photoelectric effect.
Therefore, correct order of absorb frequency is

\mathrm{K}>\mathrm{Cs}>\mathrm{Na}>\mathrm{Li}

